## Command Palette (Cmd+K)

- USE the `cmdk` package for the command palette. No custom implementations.
- The CommandPalette component lives in `src/components/CommandPalette/` co-located as usual.
- All available actions are managed through a single `useCommandRegistry` hook in `src/hooks/`. This is the only place actions are registered. The CommandPalette component reads from this hook and never defines actions itself.
- Adding a new action to Cmd+K = adding one entry to the registry. NEVER touch the palette component to add actions.
- **Every action in the app that can be performed via mouse or keyboard MUST have a Cmd+K analog.** Navigation, filters, toggles, theme switching, modals, exports — if the user can click it, they can Cmd+K it. No exceptions.
- The palette must show a **frequently used** section at the top based on usage history. Track command frequency in local state or localStorage and surface the top 5-8 most used commands as a default view when the palette opens with an empty query.
- A dedicated **help screen** (triggered via `Cmd+K → ?` or a dedicated shortcut like `Cmd+/`) must list all available commands grouped logically with their keyboard shortcuts.
- **Keyboard shortcuts must be visible on the UI surface** wherever applicable — in buttons, menu items, tooltips, sidebar links — styled inline the way Linear and Notion do it. Small, muted, right-aligned `kbd` elements showing the shortcut next to the action label. These must be theme aware.
- Style with CSS Modules. Must be theme aware. Must look premium on both light and dark.
- The palette must be accessible — full keyboard navigation, screen reader support, focus restoration on close. `cmdk` handles this out of the box, DO NOT override or break it.
- Async search results (e.g. searching pages, API-backed results) must show a loading state and stream results in as they resolve. NEVER block the input.

### Cmd+K Registration Reminder

When you create ANY new user-facing action (button, toggle, navigation link, filter, modal trigger, export action), you MUST also add a corresponding entry in `useCommandRegistry`. If you did not add the registry entry, the feature is NOT complete.
